This product is a modified version of Swiss, the homebrew utility for the
Nintendo GameCube:

    Swiss — https://github.com/emukidid/swiss-gc
    Copyright (c) emukidid and the Swiss contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

Indigo keeps that licence. The modifications in this repository are the
interface: an animated four-face Home, a retained poster library, game
details, a rebuilt Settings and System surface, shared controller navigation,
and the cheat presentation around them. The device handlers, patch engine and
loader are upstream's work.

This is an unofficial fork. It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or
supported by the Swiss project, and issues found here should not be reported
upstream.

The Library's Spotlight layout, a game's gameplay still and details above a
row of disc banners, takes its design from Gameplay Spotlight, a
gameplay-first GameCube launcher by mvizensk, with its author's permission:

    Gameplay Spotlight — https://github.com/mvizensk/gameplay-spotlight
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.

Indigo's code for the layout is its own. System › Credits thanks mvizensk too.

Memory Cards' save cubes are sized, coloured and moved by the GameCube's own
Memory Card screen as Cubeboot and Gameplay Spotlight document it from their
study of the console's menu: how far the highlighted cube sways and how
fast, how much it grows, and how big an empty cube and an icon are beside a
save's cube. Indigo's code for the screen is its own; nothing of either is
copied.

    Cubeboot — https://github.com/OffBroadway/cubeboot

